@host = http://localhost:5080

### 1. Health (should return Healthy when the database is reachable)
GET {{host}}/api/health

### 2. Register a normal user (run once; a second run returns 409 "already exists")
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Test User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "Str0ng#Passw0rd"
}

### 3. Login as the normal user (run this BEFORE requests 4, 5 and 9)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "Str0ng#Passw0rd"
}

### 4. Current user (send request 3 first)
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 5. Admin route as a normal user -> expect 403 (send request 3 first)
GET {{host}}/api/admin/ping
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 6. Login as the seeded admin (use the email/password from your secrets.json)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Use-A-Strong#Pass1"
}

### 7. Admin route as admin -> expect 200 (send request 6 first)
GET {{host}}/api/admin/ping
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 8. Forgot password (always returns 200)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "test@example.com" }

### 9. Update profile (send request 3 first)
PUT {{host}}/api/users/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Test User Updated" }